  "controlsRationale": "Original Space releases advance the startup and welcome screen. Arrow releases select a menu/board column; Enter drops the active player piece. Panel keeps the board, turn timer and artwork unobscured.",
  "sourcePatches": [
    {
      "path": "SOURCE_PATCH.diff",
      "files": [
        {
          "file": "code/keyboard.c",
          "originalSha256": "565e7b61ee7108439e1574694439c721d6ce3b895c7d33b1297093148b96dc98",
          "patchedSha256": "1a96612df4661f03fbc7e96ac22c9619ad86a6b41e04ea1e380edfdd41b8c4d4",
          "reason": "Consume the notified keyboard byte once, after dispatch, and return0 for unrelated notifications in both interrupt handlers. Preserve the requested keyboard notification bit before sys_irqsetpolicy overwrites its argument with an opaque control handle.",
          "verification": "Original compiled handlers discard Space release0xb9 or return an indeterminate unrelated result. Corrected actual handlers dispatch Space0xb9/Enter0x9c with one data-port read, unrelated notifications with zero reads/result0. Real browser touch enters menu and drops alternating pieces. Actual keyboard subscription source originally returns BIT(24) after requesting notify9, assertion RED; corrected source returns BIT(9) while enable/disable/remove all receive returned handle24."
        },
        {
          "file": "code/interface.c",
          "originalSha256": "d854dd9b69d24205169669dfbfae5fa6d0fd114e067764a97bd4a426ebb2bd63",
          "patchedSha256": "484b4c78cd264306577764bb90246da1bdf1a8d3f5835ef8fbc20ddd0c272626",
          "reason": "Include the owning keyboard.h before calling its char-returning menu selectors; implicit int declarations have an incompatible function ABI.",
          "verification": "Original actual interface.c plus owning keyboard.h fails conflicting return-type declarations; browser traps at the invalid waitForArrowsMenu function-pointer bitcast. Corrected compiled real menu calls startGame once and browser touch enters the board."
        },
        {
          "file": "code/proj.c",
          "originalSha256": "54df213e87fd6d69ca8f9de47ada0895bbebb9279099efece37e9d111b911eae",
          "patchedSha256": "bad9286adb4742974039db934d9110ac5662e30ea17b0978048d78fc60e67ca5",
          "reason": "Return failure status1 when a required timer, keyboard or mouse interrupt subscription fails. The original int entry returned without a value.",
          "verification": "Original source fails required nonvoid-return diagnostics. Corrected compiled actual entry returns1 at each of three failed subscriptions, stops at that subscription and never initializes the game; actual NDK27 ARM64 source compile passes."
        },
        {
          "file": "code/video_gr.c",
          "originalSha256": "9e15abf07216124070d01b8e75966142c1947b22a87d2687a74bff1d60180d75",
          "patchedSha256": "f57da60c1ee98ca5d6e1e9b9d248165b32bd31ec81b1edf8bdc63d210278c227",
          "reason": "Return NULL from the pointer-returning graphics initializer when BIOS setup fails.",
          "verification": "Original source fails required nonvoid-return diagnostics. Corrected actual vg_init returnsNULL after failed sys_int86, without querying or mapping the framebuffer; actual NDK27 ARM64 source compile passes."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
